<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ermengol VI of Urgell</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1096">1096</a>–1154</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ermengol VI of Urgell (1096–1154), called 'of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>', was Count of Urgell in Catalonia from 1102. Raised partly in Castile, he served the Castilian kings and held lands there, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valladolid">Valladolid</a>, while extending Urgell southwards against the Muslims. In 1149 he joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramon-berenguer-iv-count-of-barcelona">Ramon Berenguer IV of Barcelona</a> in capturing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lleida">Lleida</a>, which they shared.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ermengol-vi-of-urgell.jpg" alt="Ermengol VI of Urgell" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nekto; derivative work by Rowanwindwhistler work: Rowanwindwhistler · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Comtats_catalans_1035-es.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
